WINNER: CURVCELL-SID
FIRST LISTED: cocond-markov-poincare-ot
ARGUMENT: (1) behaviour_evidence + downstream_mechanism: both ideas hang off the same measured asymmetry (E5: mean successor entropy 0.931→3.405 nats, top-1 mass 0.4375→0.0543 across quintiles; E11: same-first-prefix 0.0907 vs 0.067 permuted null), but E8 fixes where the level-1 budget already is — at K=256 only 0.0822 of canonical pairs share a cluster (negative 0.0129) against 0.3106 at K=16, and E8 states that a small K is what width-20 prefix survival depends on. cocond-markov-poincare-ot re-orders the assignment plan at a fixed K=256, i.e. at a level whose sharing rate is already 0.0907/0.0822, whereas CURVCELL-SID is a cell-radius mechanism, the exact lever E8 names, and its observable (H(next code | level-0) falling, Spearman |A_k| vs B_k > 0) is the assignment change E8 implies; the E5 spread is the per-item branching the cell sizes are built from. (2) implementability + geometry_necessity: in A step (5) "the vector passed on is log_0(c_{j*}) with a straight-through gradient from r_i", although CHANGE says only the Euclidean argmin is replaced, so the residual hand-off to levels 2..L is either code-only (those levels stop carrying item information and the SID alphabet collapses) or unspecified; alpha and q, the two knobs that set the diffusion, are declared "measured, never tuned (see SAFEGUARDS)" with no measurement rule anywhere, and the cost estimate omits the B×B×K diffusion products — A names no matched Euclidean cost, so its curvature ablation changes the metric everywhere. B specifies the Mobius recursion eps = (-c) ⊕ eps, the closed-form s_new = log(1+B)/((d-1)R), the detachment of s and the refresh, and argues the added value against behaviour-off and geometry-off. (3) falsifiability + novelty/exploration: B ships behaviour-off (field collapsed to unit curvature), geometry-off (same behaviour-derived s, Euclidean distance) and baseline, plus an internal falsifier — Spearman |A_k| vs B_k ≈ 0 means the encoder absorbed the behaviour — which separates mechanism failure from seed noise; A's own risk list concedes the single-seed protocol cannot separate those, and its only discriminators are the two post-hoc conditionals (a rises while c does not / neither rises). A is the more distinct computation (plan-level diffusion is absent from the earlier-round ledger; B is a per-code refinement of the measured per-branch-curvature family, E6 successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500, v2 0.05463, tangent_successor_residual 0.05500, all under Euclidean l1_br_euclid 0.06207), but novelty is one 20% dimension and B's geometry-off arm is precisely that Euclidean control, while A's failures fall on implementability, geometry and the level-1 headroom.
FAILURE RISK: B's behaviour signal and its curvature are the same scalar s = sqrt(kappa); s is detached and enters only as a distance divisor, so the encoder can move or shrink latents until the argmin no longer shifts and the field is a no-op, and because the cumulative mean is written with the epoch t from {1,2,4,...,2048}, the 2048 refresh carries weight 1/2048 and the field freezes on the early noisy partition; the non-metric distance can also leave cells empty or non-convex, and the loop can inflate |A_k| and B_k together so Spearman stays positive while H(next code | level-0) never falls. This choice would be wrong if A's step (5) is a typo for the standard residual (r_i ⊖ c): then A's deep-level diffusion targets the depth-4 target-SID-in-beams statistic that actually tracks recall in E6 (0.0847→0.06207, 0.0884→0.06363), and B's level-1 cell coarsening would be the wrong lever.